{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DLX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I} \\subset \\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\pi_*$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0008": "$T \\to B$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{I}_T = \\Im((Y_T \\to Y)^*\\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{O}_{Y_T})$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Cohstack_{X/B} \\to \\Cohstack_{Y/B}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\xi = (T \\to B, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{I}_T$", "MATH_0015": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0016": "$$\n\\mathcal{F} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_{Y_T}} (Y_T \\to Y)^*\\mathcal{I}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{F}\n$$", "MATH_0017": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n(Y_{T'} \\to Y_T)^*(\n\\mathcal{F} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_{Y_T}} (Y_T \\to Y)^*\\mathcal{I}) =\n(Y_{T'} \\to Y_T)^*\\mathcal{F} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_{Y_{T'}}}\n(Y_{T'} \\to Y)^*\\mathcal{I})\n$$", "MATH_0019": "$T'$", "MATH_0020": "$T$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-i-star-equivalence}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-coherent-functorial}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-flat-lemma-F-zero-closed-proper}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8292fca95d9d274b4e6e1f79c12a912454a7ffcad147eb0f4a73e48e90dc2dd9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5f4ccf346cf0efe1bbcbb99be072ae5567846e34f3d52c22174400a7341e4c87", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be the sheaf of ideals cutting\nout <MATH_0002> as a closed subspace of <MATH_0003>. Recall that <MATH_0004> induces\nan equivalence between the category of quasi-coherent <MATH_0005>-modules\nand the category of quasi-coherent <MATH_0006>-modules annihilated\nby <MATH_0007>, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nThe same, mutatis mutandis, is true after base by <MATH_0008> with\n<MATH_0009> replaced by the ideal sheaf\n<MATH_0010>.\nAnalyzing the proof of Lemma <REF_0002>\nwe find that the essential image of\n<MATH_0011>\nis exactly the objects <MATH_0012>\nwhere <MATH_0013> is annihilated by <MATH_0014>.\nIn other words, <MATH_0015> is in the essential image if and only if\nthe multiplication map\n<MATH_0016>\nis zero and similarly after any further base change <MATH_0017>.\nNote that\n<MATH_0018>\nHence the vanishing of the multiplication map on <MATH_0019>\nis representable by a closed subspace of <MATH_0020> by\nFlatness on Spaces, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:12d47fe40500d1c9c94fdbbde0b188e17409784223ed115e25214f7129dabeac", "unit_id": "tag:0DNB:proof"}
